{"causes":["The popularity of the Harry Potter series created a demand for supplementary texts that expanded the wizarding world.","The emergence of fantasy literature as a significant genre in the early 21st century influenced Rowling’s decision to explore sports in her fictional universe.","Cultural interest in sports and their societal implications prompted a deeper examination of Quidditch within the context of wizarding culture."],"effects":[""Quidditch Through the Ages" contributed to the commercial success of the Harry Potter franchise, increasing book sales and related merchandise.","The book inspired the creation of real-life Quidditch leagues, fostering community and sport among fans worldwide.","It has influenced subsequent fantasy literature by highlighting the importance of sports as a cultural element in fictional worlds."],"relationships":[{"sourceSlug":"harry-potter-series","sourceName":"Harry Potter Series","verb":"CREATES","targetSlug":"quidditch-through-the-ages","targetName":"Quidditch Through the Ages","context":"The Harry Potter series, launched in 1997, created a rich universe where Quidditch became a central cultural element, leading to the creation of this companion book."},{"sourceSlug":"world-cup","sourceName":"Quidditch World Cup","verb":"OCCURS_IN","targetSlug":"quidditch-through-the-ages","targetName":"Quidditch Through the Ages","context":"The Quidditch World Cup, a major event in the wizarding calendar, is detailed in "Quidditch Through the Ages", showcasing its cultural significance."},{"sourceSlug":"fantasy-literature","sourceName":"Fantasy Literature","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"quidditch-through-the-ages","targetName":"Quidditch Through the Ages","context":"The rise of fantasy literature influenced the creation of "Quidditch Through the Ages", emphasizing the role of sports in fictional narratives."},{"sourceSlug":"sports-culture","sourceName":"Sports Culture","verb":"DEFINES","targetSlug":"quidditch-through-the-ages","targetName":"Quidditch Through the Ages","context":""Quidditch Through the Ages" defines aspects of sports culture within the wizarding world, paralleling real-world sports dynamics."},{"sourceSlug":"j-k-rowling","sourceName":"J.K. Rowling","verb":"TRANSMITS","targetSlug":"quidditch-through-the-ages","targetName":"Quidditch Through the Ages","context":"J.K. Rowling transmits her insights on sports and community through "Quidditch Through the Ages", enriching the narrative of her wizarding world."}],"places":[{"name":"London, England","role":"Publication site"},{"name":"Scotland, United Kingdom","role":"Setting for early Quidditch history"},{"name":"Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry, Scotland","role":"Major location in Quidditch lore"}],"texts":[{"title":"Wikipedia: Quidditch Through the Ages","type":"Reference article","slug":"quidditch-through-the-ages"}],"externalLinks":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q192258","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quidditch_Through_the_Ages"],"tags":["literary work","Historical & Literary Texts","cause-and-effect"],"thumbnailUrl":"","quote":"","legacySummary":"Quidditch Through the Ages contributed to the historical record of the Classical period. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.","summary":"Quidditch Through the Ages is a companion book to the Harry Potter series by J.K. Rowling (b. 1965), published on 12 March 2001 by Bloomsbury (UK) and Scholastic (US), simultaneously with Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them. The book is presented as a real in-universe text — a copy of the book described as being found in the Hogwarts library, 'written by' Kennilworthy Whisp — that describes the history, rules, and teams of Quidditch, the fictional wizarding sport played on broomsticks. Both Quidditch Through the Ages and Fantastic Beasts were published for Comic Relief, with all author royalties donated to the charity.

Quidditch Through the Ages is an example of the 'fictional textbook' genre within the Harry Potter universe — books presented as real in-universe artefacts that expand the world of wizarding Britain by providing detailed fictional histories, taxonomies, and cultural contexts beyond what appears in the main novels. The book describes the origins of Quidditch (from a fictional historical account of broomstick games in medieval Britain), the evolution of the rules and equipment, and the thirteen principal Quidditch teams of Britain and Ireland.

The publication of Quidditch Through the Ages and Fantastic Beasts demonstrated J.K. Rowling's awareness of secondary world creation as a commercial and cultural strategy — the in-universe fictional textbook format allowed her to expand the Harry Potter world without continuing the main narrative, generating new layers of detail that deepened the immersive quality of the wizarding world for fans. The books also demonstrated the enormous commercial power of the Harry Potter brand — both sold in the millions worldwide and made substantial donations to Comic Relief. The Quidditch sport itself became one of the Harry Potter universe's most significant cultural exports, inspiring 'Muggle Quidditch' (now 'Quadball'), a real athletic sport played on university campuses worldwide with a broom between the legs.","subjects":["English Literature","21st Century","J.K. Rowling","Fantasy Literature","Harry Potter","Children's Literature","Sports Culture","Charitable Publishing"],"frameworks":["STRUCTURAL_ANALYSIS","CAUSE_AND_EFFECT"],"historicalSignificance":{"significanceScore":7,"significanceNarrative":""Quidditch Through the Ages" significantly shaped the perception of sports in fantasy literature, inspiring real-world adaptations and discussions about cultural identity.","significanceCategory":"regional"},"_editLog":[]}
